# No file is converted between LF and CRLF, on any platform: every checkout is
# byte-for-byte what the repository holds. Git for Windows converts by default
# (core.autocrlf), and that broke two things nobody on Linux could see — every test
# that reads a source or web file and looks for a line break found none, and an
# atlas.exe built from such a checkout embedded web bundles whose bytes no longer
# match the checksums recorded for them. An attribute outranks core.autocrlf, so this
# holds whatever a contributor's Git is set to. It is what the Go project does too.
* -text
